        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benthesikyme, Benthesicyme, Poseidon, Amphitrite, Enalos\n- Works: Bibliotheca\n- Concepts: Greek mythology, ancient Greek religion, Twelve Olympians, Bronze Age Greece\n- Places: Pylos, Thebes\n\nFacts:\n- In pre-Olympian Bronze Age Greece, Poseidon was venerated as a chief deity at Pylos and Thebes.\n- In ancient Greek religion and myth, Poseidon was one of the Twelve Olympians.\n- In Greek mythology, according to the Bibliotheca, Benthesikyme or Benthesicyme was a daughter of Poseidon and Amphitrite.\n- In Greek mythology, according to the Bibliotheca, Benthesikyme was the wife of Enalos and had two daughters by him.",
